# Corpus unit fre/C04 — defeated (causal; component_ablation, unmet-defeater -> within_noise undercut)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/fre.yaml C04 (causal, uncertain=true; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline:
# performance scales smoothly with reward diversity and FRE-all dominates all reward-subset
# ablations — total AntMaze score FRE-all 47.3 +- 7, the argmax over 7 variants.
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Family map: component_ablation. C = reward_diversity (joint encoding of disparate reward
#     families), S = fre_all, Q = antmaze_total_score. The 7-variant totals live in `nl`/refs.
#   * unmet-defeater path (LOWERING.md "Attacks"). FIRST checked the other mandatory CQs, since a
#     co-occurring unmet-gap would make the gap rule win instead: CQ1 discharges single_variable AND
#     protocol_parity (same budget, all other hyperparameters identical); variance_reported is MET
#     (Table 4 gives mean +- std over seeds). NONE is independently unmet-gap, so the defeater path
#     applies and the arg is declared COMPLETE.
#   * The defeater: CQ2 ("dominance supported at the reported seed variance") is unmet-defeater —
#     FRE-all 47.3 +- 7 sits only 0.4 points above FRE-goal-lin 46.9 +- 7, inside overlapping +-7
#     intervals, i.e. the margin is within noise. That is exactly the component_ablation exception
#     within_noise(C, S, Q). A leaf-rooted challenge concludes within_noise and undercuts a1 at the
#     rule (contesting the variance_reported discharge — the paper's own claimed basis for the
#     ordering). The undercutter is unattacked, so a1 is out and the claim is defeated: the paper's
#     own Table 4 numbers defeat the strict "dominates all subsets" reading (the weaker single-family
#     falsification criterion still passes; annotation uncertain=true on gap-vs-defeater — defeater
#     chosen because the table actively contradicts strict dominance rather than merely omitting a
#     test). Optional CQs (sample-count confound met; scaling-smoothness trend unmet) omitted.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact fre at sha256:c1bb86743873
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim ------------------------------------------------------------------------

claim c04
  nl      = "On AntMaze, performance scales smoothly with reward diversity and FRE-all dominates all reward-subset ablations — total score FRE-all 47.3 +- 7 is the argmax over the 7 variants"
  formal  = contributes(reward_diversity, fre_all, antmaze_total_score)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

leaf e1 : reports(e03, ablation_effect(reward_diversity, fre_all, antmaze_total_score, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/tables/table4_reward_subset_ablation.md, Table-4-row-total]

leaf e2 : isolated(reward_diversity, e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-step-2]

leaf e3 : matched_protocol(e03)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E03-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-step-2]

leaf e4 : variance_reported(e03)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/tables/table4_reward_subset_ablation.md, Table-4-row-total]

# The defeater: FRE-all 47.3 +- 7 vs FRE-goal-lin 46.9 +- 7 — a 0.4-point argmax inside overlapping
# +-7 seed intervals, so the strict-dominance ordering is within noise.
leaf u1 : within_noise(reward_diversity, fre_all, antmaze_total_score)
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/tables/table4_reward_subset_ablation.md, Table-4-row-total, evidence/figures/figure5_reward_diversity_scaling.md]

# --- The support argument ----------------------------------------------------------------------

arg a1 : supports(c04) by component_ablation(reward_diversity, fre_all, antmaze_total_score, e03)
  discharge single_variable   with e2
  discharge protocol_parity   with e3
  discharge variance_reported with e4

# --- The paper's own overlapping intervals undercut the dominance ------------------------------

# Licensed by `exception component_ablation : within_noise(C, S, Q)` (corpus-v1). The challenge
# contests the variance_reported discharge — the reported +-7 seed intervals overlap, so they do
# not support the 0.4-point strict-dominance ordering.
arg d1 : challenges(variance_reported(a1)) by leaf(u1)
undercut d1 a1.rule

status c04

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF (declaration order): a1, d1.
#   d1 -> in  (leaf-rooted, unattacked)
#   a1 -> out (undercut by d1; undercuts always succeed, spec §7)
# Claim status:
#   c04 -> defeated (its only support a1 is `out`; spec §8 aggregation)
